WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:08.928
One day Robin Hood had a special task for Little John.

2
00:00:08.929 --> 00:00:11.353
"It's time for a feast.

3
00:00:11.354 --> 00:00:15.827
Take some men and find a wealthy guest," said Robin.

4
00:00:15.828 --> 00:00:18.826
Little John clapped his hands with delight.

5
00:00:18.827 --> 00:00:25.323
"Don't worry. We won't return without a guest."

6
00:00:25.324 --> 00:00:29.449
Soon he and his men were heading east.

7
00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:36.203
Meanwhile Robin decided to look for a guest too.

8
00:00:36.204 --> 00:00:40.581
He went west with his own group of men.

9
00:00:40.582 --> 00:00:47.788
They left Sherwood Forest and wandered through open fields.

10
00:00:47.789 --> 00:00:52.841
They traveled along the main roads and through villages.

11
00:00:52.842 --> 00:00:57.881
But they didn't find anyone worth bringing back to the forest.

12
00:00:57.882 --> 00:01:02.545
At last they came to a spot where two roads crossed.

13
00:01:02.546 --> 00:01:05.622
A high hedge bordered the roads.

14
00:01:05.623 --> 00:01:09.164
"Let's stop here and have lunch," said Robin.

15
00:01:09.165 --> 00:01:14.147
"We can hide behind the hedge and see anyone who passes."

16
00:01:14.148 --> 00:01:18.330
The men pulled bread and meat from their bags.

17
00:01:18.331 --> 00:01:22.499
They watched the roads as they ate.

18
00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:26.845
Finally a man came slowly riding toward them.

19
00:01:26.846 --> 00:01:30.833
He was wearing fine clothing and appeared to be a rich knight.

20
00:01:30.834 --> 00:01:37.469
But unlike most knights, he wasn't wearing a gold chain around his neck.

21
00:01:37.470 --> 00:01:41.284
His head was bowed and his arms hung at his sides.

22
00:01:41.285 --> 00:01:44.583
His horse walked with its head bowed too.

23
00:01:44.584 --> 00:01:47.535
They both seemed very sad.

24
00:01:47.536 --> 00:01:51.436
"This is not the usual knight," whispered Robin.

25
00:01:51.437 --> 00:01:55.499
"But we may get some money from him anyway."

26
00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:58.734
Robin waited for the man to come closer.

27
00:01:58.735 --> 00:02:03.056
Then he stepped into the road and grabbed the horse's reins.

28
00:02:03.057 --> 00:02:07.166
"Hello, sir! Stop for a few moments and chat with me."

29
00:02:07.167 --> 00:02:11.603
"Why are you stopping me?" The knight was startled. "Who are you?"

30
00:02:11.604 --> 00:02:16.809
"It depends upon whom you ask," said Robin with a merry smile.

31
00:02:16.810 --> 00:02:20.190
"Some say that I'm a good, honest fellow.

32
00:02:20.191 --> 00:02:26.246
Others call me a thief. But I call myself Robin Hood."

33
00:02:26.247 --> 00:02:30.048
"Robin Hood!" The knight smiled with relief.

34
00:02:30.049 --> 00:02:32.887
"I've heard more good things than bad about you.

35
00:02:32.888 --> 00:02:34.709
But what do you want with me?"

36
00:02:34.710 --> 00:02:39.205
"My men and I are known for our feasts in Sherwood Forest.

37
00:02:39.206 --> 00:02:43.621
We'd like to invite you to be our guest," said Robin.

38
00:02:43.622 --> 00:02:48.046
"I wouldn't be very good company," the knight muttered.

39
00:02:48.047 --> 00:02:53.115
"Nonsense! I'm sure you'll be a delightful guest," said Robin.

40
00:02:53.116 --> 00:02:56.992
"But I must warn you that our guests don't eat for free."

41
00:02:56.993 --> 00:03:05.052
At this point Robin gave a shrill whistle and his men suddenly appeared.

42
00:03:05.053 --> 00:03:08.728
"These are my men," Robin said proudly.

43
00:03:08.729 --> 00:03:11.610
They were all looking at the knight.

44
00:03:11.611 --> 00:03:16.003
"How much money are you carrying, sir?" asked Robin.

45
00:03:16.004 --> 00:03:18.715
At first the knight said nothing.

46
00:03:18.716 --> 00:03:23.955
He sat silently upon his horse while his face slowly turned red.

47
00:03:23.956 --> 00:03:27.800
Finally he said, "My name is Sir Richard.

48
00:03:27.801 --> 00:03:32.206
I'm ashamed to say that I have only ten shillings in my wallet.

49
00:03:32.207 --> 00:03:33.204
Please believe me.

50
00:03:33.205 --> 00:03:35.865
This is all the money I have in the world."

51
00:03:35.866 --> 00:03:40.226
Sir Richard held his wallet out, so that Robin could take it.

52
00:03:40.227 --> 00:03:42.646
Robin shook his head.

53
00:03:42.647 --> 00:03:44.974
"Put away your wallet.

54
00:03:44.975 --> 00:03:49.264
I would never doubt such a gentle, honest person."

55
00:03:49.265 --> 00:03:52.122
He studied the knight's face.

56
00:03:52.123 --> 00:03:54.358
"You look so sad, Sir Richard.

57
00:03:54.359 --> 00:03:56.649
Will you tell me what's troubling you?"

58
00:03:56.650 --> 00:04:02.483
The knight sighed. "I'm about to lose my castle and all my land."

59
00:04:02.484 --> 00:04:05.903
Then Sir Richard told his sad story.

60
00:04:05.904 --> 00:04:09.999
A year ago his son had participated in a joust.

61
00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:12.369
The first few matches went well.

62
00:04:12.370 --> 00:04:16.916
Then the young man had accidentally killed another man.

63
00:04:16.917 --> 00:04:20.495
The dead man had very powerful friends in the king's court.

64
00:04:20.496 --> 00:04:27.703
So Sir Richard had to pay six hundred pounds to keep his son out of prison.

65
00:04:27.704 --> 00:04:30.887
"I didn't have enough money," said Sir Richard.

66
00:04:30.888 --> 00:04:34.898
"I had no choice but to borrow money from an abbot.

67
00:04:34.899 --> 00:04:38.307
The loan is due in three days, and I can't pay.

68
00:04:38.308 --> 00:04:42.355
The monastery is going to take all my property."

69
00:04:42.356 --> 00:04:46.019
"How much money did you borrow?" asked Robin.

70
00:04:46.020 --> 00:04:50.173
"Only four hundred pounds," replied Sir Richard.

71
00:04:50.174 --> 00:04:52.674
Robin's eyes filled with anger.

72
00:04:52.675 --> 00:04:56.429
"The abbot took advantage of you during your time of need!"

73
00:04:56.430 --> 00:04:59.210
Sir Richard shrugged.

74
00:04:59.211 --> 00:05:01.587
"There was nothing else I could do."

75
00:05:01.588 --> 00:05:07.862
"Well, it's a shame to lose everything you own for just four hundred pounds," said Robin.

76
00:05:07.863 --> 00:05:10.096
"What will you do now?"

77
00:05:10.097 --> 00:05:12.540
"I'll go to Palestine to join my son.

78
00:05:12.541 --> 00:05:14.487
He's there fighting in the Crusades.

79
00:05:14.488 --> 00:05:17.921
So I won't suffer greatly from the loss of property.

80
00:05:17.922 --> 00:05:20.796
But my poor wife . . . She will be homeless."

81
00:05:20.797 --> 00:05:23.893
The knight's eyes filled with tears.

82
00:05:23.894 --> 00:05:27.411
"Perhaps her family will let her live with them."

83
00:05:27.412 --> 00:05:29.598
Robin didn't hesitate.

84
00:05:29.599 --> 00:05:34.382
"Sir Richard, you must come to Sherwood Forest with us.

85
00:05:34.383 --> 00:05:37.456
We will help you."

